Package: percona-maxscale
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Provides: maxscale (= ${binary:Version})
Conflicts: maxscale
Replaces: maxscale, maxscale-experimental (<< 6)
Description: MaxScale - An intelligent database proxy
 MariaDB MaxScale is an intelligent proxy that allows forwarding of
 database statements to one or more database servers using complex rules,
 a semantic understanding of the database statements and the roles of
 the various servers within the backend cluster of databases.
 .
 MaxScale is designed to provide load balancing and high availability
 functionality transparently to the applications. In addition it provides
 a highly scalable and flexible architecture, with plugin components to
 support different protocols and routing decisions.

Package: percona-maxscale-devel
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Depends: percona-maxscale (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Provides: maxscale-devel (= ${binary:Version})
Conflicts: maxscale-devel
Replaces: maxscale-devel
Description: MaxScale plugin development headers
 This package contains header files required for plugin module development for
 MariaDB MaxScale. The source of MariaDB MaxScale is not required.
